{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and actuation as separate plants, then use small deterministic specifications to bind sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe exploratory or recovery action. The policy favors random_walk in clear/search situations, inserts a short move_forward pulse after a successful random walk to improve coverage, and uses directed one-shot turns for obstacle recovery. Uncontrollable events are total in every specification state, with non-critical path_clear usually self-looping in action states so intended pulses are not preempted.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensor outcomes from motion capabilities in plant automata.",
    "Use one policy specification with clear/search, forward-progress, and obstacle-recovery states.",
    "Bias toward coverage by alternating random_walk and short move_forward when clear.",
    "Use rotate_clockwise for front/left obstacles and rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles.",
    "Return to exploration immediately on path_clear after recovery; reserve full_rotate and do not use it in normal exploration."
  ],
